    {
      "path": "topics/programme-ideas-20261031/ideas/candidates.md",
      "line": 442,
      "text": "- Separation criterion vs closest entry (and observation that falsifies it): vs IDEA-048: a cell mechanism and a second-order term \u2014 the cell mechanism is falsified (extra maxima are crease pairs straddling zero curves of fundamental polynomials, BDS 2026 Remark 2), the second-order term stands and is now MEASURED to 12 digits; vs LIT-030/031: optimise and identify rather than factor \u2014 falsified as a programme item by BSV 2012 (family and degree-dependent \u039b-optimal parameters, Table 5) and DU 2014 Prop. 1 (separability is a theorem); vs Kolomoitsev\u2013Lomako 2021: exact second term and argmax \u2014 a sharpening, not a renaming (adversarial-gen4-2.md (iv))."
    },
    {
      "path": "topics/programme-ideas-20261031/ideas/candidates.md",
      "line": 451,
      "text": "- Disposition and precise rejected scope, if any: retained as project proposal-1 (2\u20133 papers, not a programme), 2026-11-01. Rejected: sub-problem 2 as stated (universal lower bound \u039b \u2265 (4/\u03c0\u00b2) log\u00b2 n \u2212 C log n via the projection constant \u2014 capped at (16/\u03c0\u2074) log\u00b2 n; the generator's entry-point-4 reading rested on a bug and a wrong target constant); sub-problem 3's mechanism (\"unique critical point per Lissajous cell\"); sub-problem 4 as a paper (BSV 2012 family and parameters; DU 2014 separability; dCDM 2015 explicit energy; determinant-optimal sets have \u039b = 6.60 vs 5.92 at n = 10); the published n = 6, 7, 8 counts 39/42/56 and the adversary's 29/38 as undercounts (certified 41/50/62). Retained: Paper A (corner expansion + corner-argmax theorem), Paper B (certified counting tool + corrected table), Paper C (counting theorem with BDS, optional); the absorbed IDEA-20 negative stays a remark."
    }
  ],
